irector | Age 60 | Compensation: $2.5M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 5K people. Revenue per employee of $508K ranks in the below the sector median among Basic Materials peers, with revenue growing 14%/yr across its filed history. Stock-based compensation of $4K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 5\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (5/10).","financial_summary":["Tronox Holdings plc is a small-cap basic materials business with a $418M market cap on $2.9B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -6% over the past three years and +3% annually across the full decade, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome.","Returns on capital run at 2% against a 8% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests, and 17% gross margins are typical of commodity economics where competitors can replicate the product cheaply.","The company is burning through $281M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 61.7\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and thin -1.3\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Management returns a meaningful 11.5% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insiders hold 26% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Piotroski score 2/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.7) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Very elevated short interest (15.4% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting against the business","sev":"red","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Operating margins 18% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Carries a 124% premium to sector median EV/EBITDA","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":1.2386404724599251},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Value-trap profile (score 63/100): leveraged balance sheet under pressure; roic below cost of capital \u2014 cheapness may reflect deterioration, not mispricing","sev":"amber","cat":"value_trap"},{"text":"Carries more leverage than most Basic Materials peers \u2014 a smaller cushion for the inevitable bad year","sev":"amber","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Trade policy and tariff whiplash \u2014 materials producers are first-order casualties of protectionist swings, and margin gets squeezed from both input and output pricing.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Tronox (TROX) versus Its Competitors Head-To-Head Analysis","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/13/tronox-trox-versus-its-competitors-head-to-head-analysis.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794578332.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.844,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"UBS Group Has Lowered Expectations for Tronox (NYSE:TROX) Stock Price","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026